# Weights. VLM weights are pulled by the runtime (mlx-vlm, or the server behind
# --vlm-endpoint) into the HuggingFace cache. A multi-gigabyte weight file has
# no business in git, and one in a diff is a sign something resolved to the
# wrong directory.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
/models/

node_modules/
dist/
build/

# Bun. The lockfile is NOT ignored — this ships as a binary, so the dependency
# set has to be reproducible.
.bun/

# EXCEPT under app/, which npm manages: `app/package-lock.json` is that half's
# real lockfile. `app/bun.lock` is a byproduct of the gates — they run
# `bunx tsc` and `bunx ng build` from that directory, and bun writes a lockfile
# wherever it resolves. Ignored rather than deleted, because the next gate run
# would only write it again, and an untracked 190 kB artifact sitting in the
# way of `git add -A` is how a build's scratch ends up in somebody's history.
app/bun.lock

# Python bytecode (the VLM sidecar is Python; CPython drops these next to the source)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scratch
*.log
tmp/
.cache/

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Claude Code local state (permissions, agent worktrees)
.claude/
